The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

eltree1:

 Example program for using the eltree module
 Use eltree (quadtree) to eltree the region.
 Compute an integral on a circle or sphere for which the exact solution is known

eltree2:

 simple illustration for the use of the module submesh (part of eltree)

eltree3:

 Example program for using the eltree module
 Use eltree (quadtree) together with aligned triangles/tets near the
 interface to eltree the region.
 Compute an integral on a circle or sphere for which the exact solution is known

eltree4:

 Example program for using the eltree module
 Use eltree (quadtree/octree) together with aligned triangles/tets near the
 interface to eltree the region.
 Compute an integral on a (the boundary of a) circle or sphere for which the 
 exact solution is known

eltree5:

 Example program for using the eltree module
 A 2D region is divided into finite elements.
 Use eltree (quadtree) together with aligned triangles near the
 interface to eltree the elements.
 Compute an integral on a (the boundary of a) circle for which the exact 
 solution is known

eltree6:

 Example program for using the eltree module
 A 3D region is divided into finite elements.
 Use eltree (octtree) together with aligned tets near the
 interface to eltree the elements.
 Compute an integral on a (the boundary of a) sphere 
 for which the exact solution is known

eltree7:

 Example program for using the eltree module for triangles and tetrahedra
 Use eltree to subdivide the region and integrate over the interface of a 
 circle.

eltree8:

 Example program for using the eltree module for triangles and tetrahedra.
 Use eltree to subdivide the region and integrate over the interface of a 
 sphere.

eltree9:

 Example program for using the eltree module for triangles.
 Use eltree to subdivide the region and integrate over the volume of a 
 circle.

eltree10:

 Example program for using the eltree module for tetrahedra.
 Use eltree to subdivide the region and integrate over the volume of a 
 sphere.
